 "context": [
  {
   "h": "Cupid's warning",
   "body": "<p>From the start of the marriage Cupid had visited Psyche only at night and had warned her, more than once, never to try to see his face, or she would lose him. Her jealous sisters persuaded her that her unseen husband was a monstrous serpent who would devour her, and talked her into hiding a lamp and a razor to kill him in his sleep. When the lamp revealed Cupid himself, a drop of hot oil woke him. In this speech, as he flies off, he reminds her of those warnings and promises that the sisters will be punished.</p>"
  }
